{"currentVersion":12,"serviceItemId":"d6cb9de98ee840fb8b6504f0b2e234f5","serviceDescription":"Displays streets being cleaned today, street sweeping routes and schedule.","hasVersionedData":false,"supportsDisconnectedEditing":false,"hasStaticData":false,"hasSharedDomains":false,"maxRecordCount":2000,"maxIdsCount":1000000,"supportedQueryFormats":"JSON","supportsVCSProjection":false,"supportedExportFormats":"csv,shapefile,sqlite,geoPackage,filegdb,featureCollection,geojson,kml,excel","supportedConvertFileFormats":"JSON,PBF","supportedConvertContentFormats":"LayerEditCollection","supportedFullTextLocales":["neutral","ar-SA","bg-BG","bn-IN","ca-ES","cs-CZ","da-DK","de-DE","el-GR","en-GB","en-US","es-ES","fr-FR","gu-IN","he-IL","hi-IN","hr-HR","id-ID","is-IS","it-IT","ja-JP","kn-IN","ko-KR","lt-LT","lv-LV","ml-IN","mr-IN","ms-MY","nb-NO","nl-NL","pa-IN","pl-PL","pt-BR","pt-PT","ro-RO","ru-RU","sk-SK","sl-SI","sr-Cyrl-CS","sr-Latn-CS","sv-SE","ta-IN","te-IN","th-TH","tr-TR","uk-UA","ur-PK","vi-VN","zh-CN","zh-HK","zh-MO","zh-SG","zh-TW"],"supportsSharedTemplates":true,"hasSharedTemplates":true,"capabilities":"Query,Extract","description":"\u003cdiv\u003eIn partnership with the Seattle Department of Transportation, we regularly sweep over 90% of Seattle’s arterial streets. City crews sweep 32 night routes and seven day routes throughout the year. We add three routes during leaf season.\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003ch2\u003eWhen are crews sweeping my street?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003eOpen the \u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://seattlecitygis.maps.arcgis.com/apps/webappviewer/index.html?id=81b55d54b406409cb4af17cc891dac79\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\"\u003eStreet Sweeping App\u003c/a\u003e to learn when sweeping crews are in your area:\u003c/p\u003e\u003col\u003e\u003cli\u003eEnter your address on the map home screen\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eClick on highlighted streets near your address to view sweeping route information\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eWrite down the route numbers and next scheduled sweeping dates\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eIf you can, move your vehicle to an alternate street before the next scheduled sweep\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e&nbsp;\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003ch2\u003eBenefits of Street Sweeping\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSupport Clean Waterways\u003c/strong\u003e: Pollutants build up on streets and wash into local waterways when it rains. Sweeping removes some of this debris before it is washed down the drain. Each year, we prevent about 320,000 pounds of pollutants from potentially entering our local waterways. \u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.seattle.gov/utilities/your-services/sewer-and-drainage\" rel=\"nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer\"\u003eLearn more about how SPU works to improve stormwater quality\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eKeep neighborhoods healthy and clean\u003c/strong\u003e: Sweeping removes trash and city dirt for a more appealing place to live, work, and visit. Seattle sweeps over 26,000 miles every year to keep streets clean.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eKeep Seattle traffic moving and safe\u003c/strong\u003e: Sweeping improves car and bike lane safety and reduces flooding by clearing stormwater drains.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e&nbsp;\u003c/div\u003e","copyrightText":"City of Seattle, Seattle Public Utilities","spatialReference":{"wkid":2926,"latestWkid":2926},"initialExtent":{"xmin":1254421.5816797318,"ymin":222369.0353799664,"xmax":1286449.6390715584,"ymax":244150.260339902,"spatialReference":{"wkid":2926,"latestWkid":2926}},"fullExtent":{"xmin":1249993.20105277,"ymin":185366.6228338629,"xmax":1293484.0021853149,"ymax":271522.49581809342,"spatialReference":{"wkid":2926,"latestWkid":2926}},"allowGeometryUpdates":true,"supportsTrueCurve":true,"trueCurveSupportMode":"OGC","supportedCurveTypes":["esriGeome